(:adr
  :id "ADR-0064"
  :shortcode "D64"
  :title "Human Resonance, Reflexive Cognitive Psychology, Sociological Diffusion, Market Utility, and Real-World Business Modeling Paradigms"
  :status :active
  :date "2026-09-10"
  :cluster "agent-intelligence/human-interaction"
  :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "Traditional autonomous agent paradigms operate almost exclusively in inward-facing computational domains: syntax checking, AST refactoring, and deterministic gate evaluation. However, software and autonomous agents are fundamentally socio-technical systems that succeed or fail based on their ability to perceive, resonate with, and solve problems for real human audiences, businesses, and markets. Without formal paradigms for audience resonance, reflexive psychological analysis, jobs-to-be-done utility validation, sociological diffusion, and sustainable unit economics, agents produce technically correct artifacts that suffer from user rejection, cognitive dissonance, misaligned incentives, or commercial invalidity."
  :drivers [
    "Reflexive Theory of Mind (ToM) & Recursive Perception: Formalizing Vladimir Lefebvre's reflexive control and multi-level cognitive modeling ($R_0, R_1, R_2$) where agents model how human users model the system, anticipating friction, reactance, and interpretive drift"
    "Audience Resonance & Aesthetic Mechanics: Calibrating semantic gravity, narrative alignment, and perceptual signal-to-noise ratio (SNR >= 0.75) to ensure communications and digital artifacts attract, delight, and retain human attention"
    "Jobs-To-Be-Done (JTBD) & Problem-Solution Fit: Decomposing human needs into functional, emotional, and social jobs, establishing strict threshold checks for pain severity, switching costs, and acceptable solution constraints"
    "Behavioral Economics & Choice Architecture: Integrating Kahneman System 1 intuitive heuristics and System 2 deliberative pacing, minimizing cognitive fatigue, mitigating loss aversion, and embedding ethical Hook Model loops"
    "Sociological Network Diffusion & Memetics: Modeling memetic transmission, tribal alignment, social proof dynamics, and multi-stakeholder game theory across human organizational networks"
    "Modern Agentic Business Modeling & App Formats: Codifying value creation, delivery, and capture architectures across next-generation formats (Agentic Micro-SaaS, Headless Background Operators, Dynamic Generative VDOM Canvas, Outcome-Escrow Protocols, and A2A Marketplaces)"
  ]
  :decision "Adopt ADR-0064 (D64) establishing the comprehensive Human Resonance, Reflexive Cognitive Psychology, Sociological Diffusion, Market Utility, and Real-World Business Modeling Paradigms. Author Phase 419 / Wave 71 to formalize specialized paradigm specifications in harness/paradigms/, establish executable cognitive and reflexive evaluation suites, integrate audience resonance heuristics into agent feedback loops, and codify modern agentic business model formats."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64"]
  :tasks [
    "T419ReflexiveTheoryOfMind"
    "T419AudienceResonanceAndAesthetics"
    "T419ProblemUtilityAndJTBD"
    "T419BehavioralPsychologyAndChoice"
    "T419SociologicalDiffusionAndNetworks"
    "T419AgenticBusinessModelsAndAppFormats"
    "T419Settle"
  ]
  :outcomes [
    "Formalized reflexive Theory of Mind specification and multi-level human perception modeling in pure ASN"
    "Codified semantic resonance, narrative calibration, and aesthetic attractiveness metrics"
    "Established Jobs-To-Be-Done problem validation and acceptable solution threshold evaluation"
    "Synthesized behavioral choice architectures, cognitive pacing, and trust calibration rules"
    "Modeled sociological memetic diffusion, social proof dynamics, and multi-stakeholder game-theoretic equilibrium"
    "Codified real-world agentic business models, unit economic formulas, and emerging application formats"
  ]
  :consequences [
    (:pos "Equips autonomous agents with rigorous socio-cognitive models for human interaction, eliminating cold mechanical rejection")
    (:pos "Bridges computer science engineering with real-world market validation, behavioral economics, and sustainable monetization")
    (:pos "Provides formal homoiconic ASN schemas for business model canvases, customer journey maps, and reflexive state trees")
    (:neg "Requires maintaining psychological and market domain ontology alongside low-level AST and VFS primitives")
  ])
